{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fab6c478","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.045161,"end_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.127694","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.082533","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["> **This is the RAG variant of the Urban Observatory NL-to-SQL benchmark** — the same\n","> 150 questions (30 per tier) as `urban-observatory-nl-to-sql`, re-scored under\n","> retrieval-augmented schema delivery.\n",">\n","> | | |\n","> |---|---|\n","> | **Dataset** | `wganme/urban-observatory` — unchanged, shared with the companion study |\n","> | **What differs** | Only the **retrieval configuration**: naïve top-k, rule-augmented, and full-schema few-shot arms |\n","> | **Paper** | Alnahari, Hasanin & Jambi, *\"Schema Delivery Strategies for LLM-Based Text-to-SQL on a Narrow IoT Sensor Database\"* (in preparation) |\n","> | **Companion study** | Alnahari, Hasanin & Jambi, IEEE Access 14:139629–139642, 2026 · DOI [10.1109/ACCESS.2026.3728618](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2026.3728618) |\n",">\n","> **Sections 21–22 reproduce the paper end-to-end with no API calls** — first the five\n","> figures, then every statistic and LaTeX table the manuscript reports.\n",">\n","> **The suffix `-rag` describes the *evaluation*, not the data.** The benchmark itself\n","> is untouched: two tables suffice for 146 of the 150 questions, and `readings` is\n","> required by 118.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"107b399a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.040319,"end_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.210433","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.170114","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Newcastle Urban Observatory — NL-to-SQL Benchmark\n","\n","The papers, the dataset, and what this notebook reproduces are stated once in the\n","card above. What follows is the **operational** record: what changed, and what the\n","pipeline actually does.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## ⚠️ HOT FIX — GitHub Models retired (2026). This notebook has been patched.\n","\n","**What happened.** The published experiments (May 2026) called two hosted\n","inference providers: **GitHub Models** (19 of the 29 models — 17 in the active\n","panel plus 2 opted out earlier for persistent endpoint failures) and **Kaggle AI**\n","(`kbench`, 10 models). The GitHub Models inference endpoint has since been\n","**permanently retired** by its provider, so the guard below drops the 17 active\n","dead IDs. A live probe returns:\n","\n","```\n","GitHub Models endpoint probe -> HTTP 410 (github_models_retirement_brownout)\n","```\n","\n","HTTP **410 Gone** is permanent, not a rate limit. Every GitHub-hosted model ID\n","is dead; there is no fallback.\n","\n","**Why it broke runs.** The notebook loaded those dead IDs into `MODEL_PANEL`.\n","That passed the benchmark runner's guard, so the run started — then spent the\n","whole session cooling dead endpoints and never completed a full panel.\n","\n","**The hot fix.** Section 5 probes the endpoint once at startup. If it is not\n","HTTP 200, the GitHub model IDs are removed from `MODEL_PANEL`, the stale\n","`GITHUB_TOKEN` / `GITHUB_PAT` environment variables are cleared, and the panel is\n","left for the Kaggle AI (`kbench`) cell to populate. No other behaviour changes.\n","\n","**What this means for reproducing the paper's numbers.** The published 29-model\n","results **cannot be re-run** — those endpoints no longer exist. The stored\n","results are unaffected and remain the authoritative record:\n","\n","| Artefact | Contents |\n","|---|---|\n","| `all_experiment_results.csv` | 4,246 rows, 2,080 correct (49.0%) — 29-model archive |\n","| `rag_experiment_results.csv` | 8,100 rows — 27-model RAG panel (naïve + enhanced) |\n","\n","The **10 `kbench` models are still alive**, and they carry the entire matched\n","ten-model panel on which the RAG-vs-few-shot comparison is based. So the\n","notebook still runs end-to-end; it simply reproduces the 10-model panel rather\n","than the 29-model archive.\n","\n","> **Do not change the frozen datasets.** `urban-observatory` (raw archive) and\n","> `urban-observatory-rerun` are **DOI-registered and immutable**. Only\n","> `urban-observatory-results` (private, no DOI) may be written to.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Hot-fix log\n","\n","Cell references below are SECTION numbers, not sheet positions — the notebook has\n","been reordered since these fixes were made, so raw cell numbers would be wrong.\n","\n","| Section | Change | Reason |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| 3 (Preflight) | Made **read-only** | It used to push a 1-row placeholder to the results dataset, destroying the 4,246-row file |\n","| 5 (Model Router) | **GitHub Models retirement guard** | Endpoint returns HTTP 410; dead IDs are dropped and `kbench` repopulates the panel |\n","| 8 (Frozen Database) | Frozen DB is an **input**, not rebuilt | A live-API rebuild drifts (1,412 / 114 / ~85.7k readings) and shifts every re-scored number |\n","| 6, 13 (protobuf) | Range-pinned `>=5.29.6,<6.0` | `pip install sentence-transformers` pulled protobuf ≥6, which `kaggle-benchmarks` rejects. Never pin an exact patch: force-reinstalling under a live runtime causes a gencode/runtime skew that only a kernel restart clears |\n","| 19, 21, 22, 23 (snapshot) | Every dataset push stages the **complete** artefact set | `dataset_create_version` **replaces** the dataset, so a partial push silently deletes the rest |\n","| 23 (Packaging) | **One-click packaging** | Bundles all artefacts into a single downloadable zip |\n","\n","**Upstream reference — the published notebook version:**\n","[v12 (scriptVersionId=345968960)](https://www.kaggle.com/code/wganme/urban-observatory-benchmark?scriptVersionId=345968960)\n","— this is the version corresponding to the IEEE Access paper. The fixes above are\n","applied on top of it.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Known limitations carried forward\n","\n","1. **`_try_kbench` does not forward `max_tokens` / `temperature`.** The function\n","   accepts both, then calls `llm_obj.prompt(prompt_text)` without them, so every\n","   `kbench` model ran at provider defaults rather than the intended temperature\n","   zero. This affected the published runs and is disclosed in the paper's\n","   Limitations section. It cannot be corrected retrospectively.\n","2. **The SQLite snapshot is NOT rebuilt.** The frozen archive\n","   (`wganme/urban-observatory`, 1,411 / 112 / 87,962) is mounted read-only and\n","   verified at startup (Section 8). A live-API rebuild would drift — today it\n","   yields 1,412 sensors / 114 variables / ~85,666 readings — which shifts both\n","   accuracy and SEI, so the frozen database is required to reproduce the\n","   published figures and a mismatch raises a `[DB WARNING]`.\n","\n","3. **`all_experiment_results.csv` is post-correction.** It holds 4,246 rows /\n","   2,080 correct. An earlier, pre-correction file of the same row count with\n","   2,078 correct exists in the archive; the two are indistinguishable by row\n","   count, which is why Section 22 validates the *correct* tally and not just the\n","   length before anything is published.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9b3257d2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.040351,"end_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.291541","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.25119","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Environment, Paths and Resume\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"44d492bf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.376367Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.376006Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-20T18:36:08.412308Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-20T18:36:08.411025Z"},"papermill":{"duration":9.082122,"end_time":"2026-09-20T18:36:08.414766","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-20T18:35:59.332644","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  seeded tables/ (12 files) from urban-observatory-results\n","  seeded figures_paper2/ (10 files) from urban-observatory-results — dropped 9 foreign: fig5_per_model_slope.png, fig3_tokens.png, fig_accuracy_sei.png\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Dataset URL: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/wganme/urban-observatory-results\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  resume-seed: all_experiment_results.csv -> 4246 rows OK\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  resume-seed: rag_experiment_results.csv -> 8100 rows OK\n","  resume-seed: few_shot_rerun_kbench_results.csv -> 1500 rows OK\n","  resume-seed: n4_rho_analysis.json -> 6 keys\n","  resume-seed: experiment_b_kbench_results.csv -> 1500 rows OK\n","  resume-seed: benchmark_questions.json -> 150 keys\n","  resume-seed: downloaded from wganme/urban-observatory-results\n","Kaggle environment: WORK_ROOT = /kaggle/working (cleaned, RESUMED from all_experiment_results.csv(4246rows))\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  Kaggle dataset mounted at: /kaggle/input/datasets/wganme/urban-observatory\n","cwd            = /kaggle/working\n","DATA_EXPORT    = /kaggle/input/datasets/wganme/urban-observatory\n","ARCHIVE_BULK   = /kaggle/input/datasets/wganme/urban-observatory  (available=True)\n","Logging all output to /kaggle/working/data_export/notebook_output.log\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","_KAGGLE_USER_FALLBACK = \"wganme\"  # Kaggle username — change once here to fork\n","\n","# Environment auto-detection (Colab / Kaggle / local) and persistent paths.\n","# - Colab : mount Google Drive; FAIL LOUDLY if /content/drive/MyDrive/... missing.\n","# - Kaggle: TWO datasets must be attached —\n","#       wganme/urban-observatory          (read-only raw archive + frozen DB)\n","#       wganme/urban-observatory-results  (read-only resume-seed of the result CSVs)\n","#   Writes always go to /kaggle/working. Attach both in the notebook's\n","#   Data panel, or set them in kernel-metadata.json dataset_sources.\n","# - Local : use repo root.\n","import os\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","_IN_KAGGLE = Path('/kaggle/input').exists() and Path('/kaggle/working').exists()\n","\n","# Detect Colab by the runtime marker file, NOT by import — Kaggle ships google.colab too.\n","_IN_COLAB = (not _IN_KAGGLE) and Path('/var/colab/hostname').exists()\n","if _IN_COLAB:\n","    from google.colab import drive  # type: ignore[import-not-found]\n","\n","if _IN_COLAB:\n","    drive.mount('/content/drive')\n","    WORK_ROOT = Path('/content/drive/MyDrive/Colab Notebooks')\n","    if not WORK_ROOT.exists():\n","        raise RuntimeError(\n","            f\"Drive mounted but {WORK_ROOT} not found.\\n\"\n","            \"Refusing to save into the ephemeral /content runtime folder.\\n\"\n","            \"Create the folder in Drive or correct WORK_ROOT before continuing.\"\n","        )\n","    print(f\"Colab + Drive: WORK_ROOT = {WORK_ROOT}\")\n","elif _IN_KAGGLE:\n","    WORK_ROOT = Path('/kaggle/working')\n","    # Cleanup /kaggle/working/* on rerun so stale outputs don't pile up.\n","    # Pattern borrowed from the sparksql.ipynb reference notebook.\n","    import glob, shutil\n","    for _f in glob.glob('/kaggle/working/*'):\n","        try:\n","            if os.path.isfile(_f) or os.path.islink(_f):\n","                os.unlink(_f)\n","            elif os.path.isdir(_f):\n","                shutil.rmtree(_f)\n","        except Exception as _e:\n","            print(f\"  cleanup warn: {_f}: {_e}\")\n","    # ── Resume seed: download the LATEST version of the rolling-results\n","    #     dataset via the Kaggle API, so the benchmark loop picks up where\n","    #     the previous session left off instead of starting from scratch.\n","    #     Fallback: also scan /kaggle/input in case the dataset is attached\n","    #     as a kernel input (mount is pinned to the version at session start).\n","    _seeded = []\n","    # Every artefact the figures consume. The first two are the benchmark arms;\n","    # the last two are NOT produced by this notebook (there is no few-shot\n","    # re-run, and SEI is computed offline), so they must be seeded from the\n","    # dataset or the mounted archive or Figure 2 cannot be built at all.\n","    _RESULT_CSVS = [\n","        \"all_experiment_results.csv\",\n","        \"rag_experiment_results.csv\",\n","        \"few_shot_rerun_kbench_results.csv\",\n","        \"n4_rho_analysis.json\",\n","        \"experiment_b_kbench_results.csv\",\n","        \"benchmark_questions.json\",\n","    ]\n","    _export_dir = WORK_ROOT / 'data_export'\n","    _export_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","    # ── Seed the heavy deliverable DIRECTORY artefacts ───────────────────────\n","    # `dataset_create_version` publishes the staging folder AS the new version,\n","    # so anything a pusher does not stage is DELETED from the dataset. The\n","    # periodic pusher fires DURING the benchmark loop, long before Sections 21\n","    # and 22 have produced tables/ and figures_paper2/ — so those directories\n","    # must already be on disk when the first mid-run push happens, or that push\n","    # wipes them. Seeding them here is what makes the carry-forward possible.\n","    # The source must be the RESULTS dataset specifically. A blind\n","    # `rglob(\"tables/\")` over /kaggle/input returns whichever directory the\n","    # filesystem happens to list first — and wganme/urban-observatory ALSO\n","    # holds a tables/ directory, from the COMPANION study (tab_fisher,\n","    # tab_mann_whitney, tab_kruskal_wallis, ...). Seeding from there replaced\n","    # this paper's twelve tables with the companion study's set.\n","    _RES_SUBDIRS = {\n","        \"tables\": {\n","            \"tab_strategy_accuracy.tex\", \"tab_tier_accuracy.tex\",\n","            \"tab_error_breakdown.tex\", \"tab_tier_correction.tex\",\n","            \"tab_paired_comparisons.tex\", \"tab_zero_shot_coverage.tex\",\n","            \"tab_snapshot.tex\", \"tab_tables_referenced.tex\",\n","            \"tab_panel_ids.tex\", \"tab_strategy_composition.tex\",\n","            \"tab_notation.tex\", \"tab_tier_taxonomy.tex\",\n","        },\n","        \"figures_paper2\": {\n","            \"fig1_pipeline.pdf\", \"fig2_tier_accuracy_and_net.pdf\",\n","            \"fig3_tokens.pdf\", \"fig4_tables_delivered.pdf\",\n","            \"fig5_per_model_slope.pdf\", \"fig_accuracy_sei.pdf\",\n","            \"fig_prompt_tokens.pdf\", \"fig_cost_accuracy.pdf\",\n","            \"paper2_figure_values.json\", \"paper2_statistics.json\",\n","        },\n","    }\n","    _res_roots = []\n","    _kin = Path('/kaggle/input')\n","    if _kin.exists():\n","        try:\n","            _res_roots = [p for p in _kin.rglob('urban-observatory-results')\n","                          if p.is_dir()]\n","        except OSError:\n","            _res_roots = []\n","    if not _res_roots:\n","        print(\"  seed note: urban-observatory-results is not mounted; the \"\n","              \"deliverable directories will be produced by Sections 21-22.\")\n","    for _sub, _known in _RES_SUBDIRS.items():\n","        _dst_d = _export_dir / _sub\n","        if _dst_d.is_dir() and any(_dst_d.iterdir()):\n","            continue\n","        for _root in _res_roots:\n","            _hit = _root / _sub\n","            if not _hit.is_dir():\n","                continue\n","            shutil.copytree(_hit, _dst_d, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n","            # Drop any file that is not part of THIS paper's set. The dataset\n","            # may legitimately hold companion-study artefacts; publishing them\n","            # from here would misattribute them.\n","            _foreign = [p for p in _dst_d.iterdir()\n","                        if p.is_file() and p.name not in _known]\n","            for _p in _foreign:\n","                _p.unlink()\n","            print(f\"  seeded {_sub}/ ({len(list(_dst_d.iterdir()))} files) from \"\n","                  f\"{_root.name}\"\n","                  + (f\" — dropped {len(_foreign)} foreign: \"\n","                     f\"{', '.join(p.name for p in _foreign[:3])}\"\n","                     if _foreign else \"\"))\n","            break\n","\n","    # ── Validation, defined at first use ──────────────────────────────────────\n","    # Section 1 seeds result files BEFORE the section that originally defined\n","    # these helpers, so calling them here raised\n","    #   \"NameError: name '_validate_results_csv' is not defined\"\n","    # which the API-download try/except swallowed. The seed then fell through to\n","    # the /kaggle/input mount — which is pinned to the version present when the\n","    # session STARTED, so a file published mid-session can never be seen. That is\n","    # why this cell reported \"RESUMED from mount:...\" while the API download had\n","    # in fact failed. The functions are defined here now.\n","    _PUBLISHED_RESULTS = {\n","        \"all_experiment_results.csv\": {\"rows\": 4246, \"correct\": 2080},\n","        \"rag_experiment_results.csv\": {\"rows\": 8100, \"correct\": 3875},\n","    }\n","\n","    def _csv_true_rows(path) -> int:\n","        \"\"\"CSV record count. NOT a line count: question and SQL fields contain\n","        embedded newlines, which inflates a line count by ~10x.\"\"\"\n","        import csv as _csv\n","        with open(path, newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as _fh:\n","            return max(0, sum(1 for _ in _csv.reader(_fh)) - 1)\n","\n","    def _validate_results_csv(path):\n","        \"\"\"Return (ok, detail) against the published expectations.\n","\n","        A filename with no expectation passes, so this never blocks an artefact\n","        it does not know about.\n","        \"\"\"\n","        import pandas as _pd\n","        _exp = _PUBLISHED_RESULTS.get(getattr(path, \"name\", str(path)))\n","        if _exp is None:\n","            return True, \"no expectation registered\"\n","        try:\n","            _n = _csv_true_rows(path)\n","            _df = _pd.read_csv(path)\n","            _c = int(_pd.to_numeric(_df.get(\"correct\", 0),\n","                                    errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0).sum())\n","        except Exception as _e:\n","            return False, f\"unreadable: {type(_e).__name__}: {_e}\"\n","        if _n != _exp[\"rows\"] or _c != _exp[\"correct\"]:\n","            return False, (f\"{_n:,} rows / {_c:,} correct, but the published \"\n","                           f\"artefact is {_exp['rows']:,} / {_exp['correct']:,}\")\n","        return True, f\"{_n:,} rows / {_c:,} correct\"\n","    # ── Primary: fetch latest via API (always up-to-date) ────────────────\n","    try:\n","        import subprocess as _seed_subp, sys as _seed_sys, zipfile as _seed_zip, tempfile as _seed_tmp\n","        # Ensure kaggle package is available\n","        try:\n","            from kaggle.api.kaggle_api_extended import KaggleApi as _SeedKaggleApi\n","        except ModuleNotFoundError:\n","            _seed_subp.run(\n","                [_seed_sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"--upgrade\", \"kaggle\"],\n","                capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180,\n","            )\n","            for _k in [k for k in list(_seed_sys.modules) if k == \"kaggle\" or k.startswith(\"kaggle.\")]:\n","                _seed_sys.modules.pop(_k, None)\n","            from kaggle.api.kaggle_api_extended import KaggleApi as _SeedKaggleApi\n","        # Bridge auth\n","        if os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_API_TOKEN\") and not os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_KEY\"):\n","            os.environ[\"KAGGLE_KEY\"] = os.environ[\"KAGGLE_API_TOKEN\"]\n","        if not os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_USERNAME\"):\n","            os.environ[\"KAGGLE_USERNAME\"] = _KAGGLE_USER_FALLBACK\n","        _api = _SeedKaggleApi(); _api.authenticate()\n","        _user = os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_USERNAME\", _KAGGLE_USER_FALLBACK)\n","        _slug = \"urban-observatory-results\"\n","        with _seed_tmp.TemporaryDirectory() as _td:\n","            _api.dataset_download_files(\n","                dataset=f\"{_user}/{_slug}\",\n","                path=_td,\n","                unzip=True,\n","                quiet=True,\n","            )\n","            _dl = Path(_td)\n","            for _csv_name in _RESULT_CSVS:\n","                _dst = _export_dir / _csv_name\n","                _candidates = list(_dl.rglob(_csv_name))\n","                if _candidates:\n","                    shutil.copy2(_candidates[0], _dst)\n","                    # Count true CSV records. A line count overstates this by\n","                    # ~10x because question/SQL fields contain embedded newlines\n","                    # (45,033 lines for a 4,246-row file).\n","                    if _csv_name.endswith(\".csv\"):\n","                        import csv as _csv\n","                        with open(_dst, newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\",\n","                                  errors=\"replace\") as _fh:\n","                            _n = max(0, sum(1 for _ in _csv.reader(_fh)) - 1)\n","                        _unit = \"rows\"\n","                    else:\n","                        import json as _json\n","                        _n = len(_json.load(open(_dst, encoding=\"utf-8\")))\n","                        _unit = \"keys\"\n","                    # Validate BEFORE trusting it. 2,078 and 2,080 are BOTH\n","                    # 4,246 rows, so a row count cannot catch the pre-correction\n","                    # file — and this seed is what the rolling snapshot later\n","                    # republishes to the dataset.\n","                    if _csv_name.endswith(\".csv\"):\n","                        _ok, _detail = _validate_results_csv(_dst)\n","                        if not _ok:\n","                            print(f\"  resume-seed: {_csv_name} FAILED validation \"\n","                                  f\"({_detail})\")\n","                            print(\"     -> NOT seeded; the published artefact differs.\")\n","                            _dst.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n","                            continue\n","                        _seeded.append(f\"{_csv_name}({_n}{_unit})\")\n","                        print(f\"  resume-seed: {_csv_name} -> {_n} {_unit} OK\")\n","                    else:\n","                        _seeded.append(f\"{_csv_name}({_n}{_unit})\")\n","                        print(f\"  resume-seed: {_csv_name} -> {_n} {_unit}\")\n","            if _seeded:\n","                print(f\"  resume-seed: downloaded from {_user}/{_slug}\")\n","    except Exception as _api_e:\n","        print(f\"  resume-seed: API download failed ({type(_api_e).__name__}: {_api_e})\")\n","    # ── Fallback: scan /kaggle/input mount (pinned at session-start version) ─\n","    if not _seeded:\n","        _kin = Path('/kaggle/input')\n","        if _kin.exists():\n","            for _csv_name in _RESULT_CSVS:\n","                _dst = _export_dir / _csv_name\n","                if _dst.exists():\n","                    continue\n","                for _src in _kin.rglob(_csv_name):\n","                    try:\n","                        shutil.copy2(_src, _dst)\n","                        _seeded.append(f\"mount:{_src}\")\n","                        break\n","                    except Exception as _e:\n","                        print(f\"  resume-seed warn: {_src}: {_e}\")\n","    if _seeded:\n","        print(f\"Kaggle environment: WORK_ROOT = {WORK_ROOT} (cleaned, RESUMED from {_seeded[0]})\")\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"Kaggle environment: WORK_ROOT = {WORK_ROOT} (cleaned, no prior results to resume)\")\n","else:\n","    WORK_ROOT = Path('/home/bcdr/Documents/phd')\n","    print(f\"Local environment: WORK_ROOT = {WORK_ROOT}\")\n","\n","os.chdir(WORK_ROOT)\n","if _IN_KAGGLE:\n","    # Read-only Kaggle dataset mount; the dataset can sit at any of these locations\n","    # depending on how it's attached. Search candidates in priority order.\n","    _kin = Path('/kaggle/input')\n","    _candidates = [\n","        _kin / 'urban-observatory',\n","        _kin / 'datasets' / _KAGGLE_USER_FALLBACK / 'urban-observatory',\n","    ]\n","    # Add anything else that contains urban_observatory.db (catches custom mount paths).\n","    if _kin.exists():\n","        for _hit in _kin.rglob('urban_observatory.db'):\n","            _candidates.append(_hit.parent)\n","    DATA_EXPORT = next((p for p in _candidates if p.exists()), None)\n","    if DATA_EXPORT is None:\n","        DATA_EXPORT = WORK_ROOT / \"data_export\"\n","        DATA_EXPORT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","        print(\"  WARNING: no dataset attached at /kaggle/input. \"\n","              f\"Attach '{_KAGGLE_USER_FALLBACK}/urban-observatory' via Add Data > Your Datasets.\")\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"  Kaggle dataset mounted at: {DATA_EXPORT}\")\n","else:\n","    DATA_EXPORT = WORK_ROOT / \"data_export\"\n","    DATA_EXPORT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=T