uestion SEI lives in\n","> `n4_rho_analysis.json`. Figure 4a therefore uses the **`prompt_tokens` delta**\n","> between the naive and rule-augmented arms, which is the only faithful trace of\n","> whether a third table was actually delivered.\n","\n","Also writes `tab_paper2_tier.tex` and `paper2_figure_values.json`, so every value\n","plotted — plus the exact McNemar contrasts — is recoverable from the repository,\n","and a `[DB WARNING]` if the database is not the frozen snapshot.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"b6a78a0f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-20T18:54:25.900993Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-20T18:54:25.900339Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-20T18:54:31.956941Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-20T18:54:31.955773Z"},"papermill":{"duration":6.113258,"end_time":"2026-09-20T18:54:31.959123","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-20T18:54:25.845865","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["inputs  : rag=OK  few_shot=OK  n4_rho=OK\n","panels  : ten-model n=10 | rag n=27\n","figures : Fig1 yes · Fig3 yes · Fig4 yes · Fig5 yes · Fig2 yes\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[figures] manuscript-named copies: fig_prompt_tokens.pdf, fig_cost_accuracy.pdf\n","\n","── Paired McNemar (exact, ten-model panel) ──\n","  T1      rule_vs_naive b=  7 c=  3 p=0.3438  OR=2.33\n","  T1      rule_vs_few   b=  6 c= 15 p=0.07835  OR=0.40\n","  T1      naive_vs_few  b=  4 c= 17 p=0.007197  OR=0.24\n","  T2      rule_vs_naive b=  7 c=  6 p=1  OR=1.17\n","  T2      rule_vs_few   b= 23 c=  5 p=0.0009122  OR=4.60\n","  T2      naive_vs_few  b= 24 c=  7 p=0.003327  OR=3.43\n","  T3      rule_vs_naive b=  8 c=  4 p=0.3877  OR=2.00\n","  T3      rule_vs_few   b= 13 c=  6 p=0.1671  OR=2.17\n","  T3      naive_vs_few  b= 12 c=  9 p=0.6636  OR=1.33\n","  T4      rule_vs_naive b= 13 c= 13 p=1  OR=1.00\n","  T4      rule_vs_few   b= 33 c= 15 p=0.01328  OR=2.20\n","  T4      naive_vs_few  b= 28 c= 10 p=0.005098  OR=2.80\n","  T5      rule_vs_naive b= 27 c=  6 p=0.0003241  OR=4.50\n","  T5      rule_vs_few   b= 30 c=  6 p=6.96e-05  OR=5.00\n","  T5      naive_vs_few  b= 26 c= 23 p=0.7754  OR=1.13\n","  overall rule_vs_naive b= 62 c= 32 p=0.002587  OR=1.94\n","  overall rule_vs_few   b=105 c= 47 p=2.9e-06  OR=2.23\n","  overall naive_vs_few  b= 94 c= 66 p=0.03247  OR=1.42\n","\n","  Tier-5 advantage (27 pairs) comes from 7 distinct questions\n","  Mean prompt tokens: naive 186  rule 219\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","[DB OK] frozen snapshot confirmed: {'sensors': 1411, 'variables': 112, 'readings': 87962}\n","\n","figures -> /kaggle/working/data_export/figures_paper2\n","  fig1_pipeline.pdf                    25,224 B\n","  fig2_tier_accuracy_and_net.pdf       18,674 B\n","  fig3_tokens.pdf                      16,362 B\n","  fig4_tables_delivered.pdf            24,911 B\n","  fig5_per_model_slope.pdf             28,061 B\n","  fig_accuracy_sei.pdf                 21,162 B\n","  fig_cost_accuracy.pdf                28,061 B\n","  fig_prompt_tokens.pdf                16,362 B\n","\n","── FIG 2a  accuracy by tier (ten-model, n=300/tier) ──\n","  T1  few  77.7   naive  73.3   rule  74.7\n","  T2  few  58.0   naive  63.7   rule  64.0\n","  T3  few  38.3   naive  39.3   rule  40.7\n","  T4  few  41.7   naive  47.7   rule  47.7\n","  T5  few  23.0   naive  24.0   rule  31.0\n","\n","── FIG 2b  net additional correct pairs (of 300) ──\n","  T1  vs naive  +4   vs few-shot  -9\n","  T2  vs naive  +1   vs few-shot +18\n","  T3  vs naive  +4   vs few-shot  +7\n","  T4  vs naive  +0   vs few-shot +18\n","  T5  vs naive +21   vs few-shot +24\n","\n","── FIG 4a  tables delivered by rule-augmented ──\n","  T1  two 26   three  4\n","  T2  two 16   three 14\n","  T3  two  9   three 21\n","  T4  two 20   three 10\n","  T5  two  4   three 26\n","\n","── FIG 5  {'better': 22, 'same': 2, 'worse': 3}, mean +1.85 pp, max +4.67, min -2.67 ──\n","\n","[OK] paper-2 figures complete (fig1, fig3, fig4, fig5, fig2) — no API calls made.\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# SECTION 21 — PAPER 2 FIGURES  (RAG / schema-delivery strategies)\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# Produces exactly the FIVE figures of\n","#   \"Schema Delivery Strategies for LLM-Based Text-to-SQL on a Narrow IoT\n","#    Sensor Database\"  (paper 2, in preparation)\n","# from data already on disk. NO API calls.\n","#\n","#   Fig 1  evaluation pipeline schematic (4 arms)          -> schematic()\n","#   Fig 2  (a) accuracy by tier x strategy, 95% Wilson CI  -> fig2a()\n","#          (b) net additional correct pairs, vs naive & few-shot\n","#   Fig 3  mean schema-context tokens by tier, +/-1 SD, bare-DDL reference line\n","#   Fig 4  (a) questions delivered 2 vs 3 tables, by tier\n","#          (b) rule-augmented accuracy by tier x tables-delivered\n","#   Fig 5  per-model slopegraph, naive -> rule-augmented (27-model panel)\n","#\n","# PANEL DISCIPLINE — this is the main trap in this dataset:\n","#   Fig 2a/2b  : TEN-model matched panel (the 10 kbench models, n=300/tier)\n","#   Fig 3/4/5  : TWENTY-SEVEN-model RAG panel (n=810/tier)\n","#   Using the wrong panel silently reproduces the wrong magnitudes.\n","#\n","# sei in the CSV is 1.0 for EVERY row (dead column). Per-question SEI\n","# lives in n4_rho_analysis.json. Fig 4a uses the prompt_tokens delta, which is\n","# the only faithful trace of whether a third table was actually delivered.\n","#\n","# Output: <WORK_ROOT>/data_export/figures_paper2/*.pdf  (+ .png previews)\n","import json\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","# The plotting stack is installed in Section 7. Guard the import so a missing\n","# matplotlib degrades to a clear message instead of aborting the whole notebook.\n","try:\n","    import matplotlib\n","    matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n","    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","except Exception as _mpl_err:\n","    raise SystemExit(\n","        f\"\\n[figures] matplotlib is not available ({type(_mpl_err).__name__}: {_mpl_err}).\\n\"\n","        \"  Section 7 installs it; re-run that cell, then this one.\\n\"\n","        \"  The result artefacts and the zip from Section 23 are unaffected.\"\n","    )\n","from matplotlib.patches import FancyArrowPatch, FancyBboxPatch\n","\n","# ── house style ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","plt.rcParams.update({\n","    \"pdf.fonttype\": 42, \"ps.fonttype\": 42, \"font.family\": \"DejaVu Sans\",\n","    \"font.size\": 9, \"axes.labelsize\": 9, \"axes.titlesize\": 10,\n","    \"legend.fontsize\": 8, \"xtick.labelsize\": 8.5, \"ytick.labelsize\": 8.5,\n","    \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n","    \"figure.dpi\": 160, \"savefig.bbox\": \"tight\", \"savefig.dpi\": 300,\n","})\n","C_FEW, C_NAIVE, C_RULE = \"#7f7f7f\", \"#4c72b0\", \"#c44e52\"\n","TIERS = [\"T1\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"T4\", \"T5\"]\n","TIER_LBL = [\"T1\\nsimple\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"T4\", \"T5\\ncomplex\"]\n","\n","_ROOT = Path(globals().get(\"WORK_ROOT\", \".\"))\n","_FIG = _ROOT / \"data_export\" / \"figures_paper2\"\n","_FIG.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","# ── resolve inputs without relying on cell ordering ──────────────────────────\n","_SKIP_DIRS = {\".git\", \"__pycache__\", \"archive_bulk\", \"node_modules\",\n","              \".virtual_documents\", \".ipynb_checkpoints\"}\n","\n","\n","def _try_find(name: str):\n","    \"\"\"Locate a data file; return None when it is genuinely unavailable.\n","\n","    Availability differs by environment, so a missing file must NOT abort the\n","    section — a Kaggle run with only the two result CSVs still yields Fig 1, 4\n","    and 5. Callers check for None and report which figures they can build.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    for c in (_ROOT / name, _ROOT / \"data_export\" / name,\n","              _ROOT / \"data_export\" / \"data_export\" / name, Path(name)):\n","        if c.exists() and c.stat().st_size > 1_000:\n","            return c\n","    stack = [(Path(_ROOT), 0)]\n","    seen = set()\n","    while stack:\n","        d, depth = stack.pop(0)\n","        if depth > 5 or str(d) in seen:\n","            continue\n","        seen.add(str(d))\n","        try:\n","            entries = sorted(d.iterdir())\n","        except (OSError, PermissionError):\n","            continue\n","        for e in entries:\n","            if e.is_file() and e.name == name and e.stat().st_size > 1_000:\n","                return e\n","            if e.is_dir() and e.name not in _SKIP_DIRS and not e.is_symlink():\n","                stack.append((e, depth + 1))\n","    return None\n","\n","\n","_RAG_P = _try_find(\"rag_experiment_results.csv\")\n","_FEW_P = _try_find(\"few_shot_rerun_kbench_results.csv\")\n","_SEI_P = _try_find(\"n4_rho_analysis.json\")\n","\n","HAVE = {\"rag\": _RAG_P is not None, \"few\": _FEW_P is not None, \"SEI\": _SEI_P is not None}\n","print(f\"inputs  : rag={'OK' if HAVE['rag'] else 'MISSING'}  \"\n","      f\"few_shot={'OK' if HAVE['few'] else 'MISSING'}  \"\n","      f\"n4_rho={'OK' if HAVE['SEI'] else 'MISSING'}\")\n","\n","if not HAVE[\"rag\"]:\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(\n","        \"rag_experiment_results.csv is REQUIRED (every figure except Fig 1 uses it).\\n\"\n","        \"Attach wganme/urban-observatory-results, or run the RAG cells first.\"\n","    )\n","\n","rag = pd.read_csv(_RAG_P)\n","few = pd.read_csv(_FEW_P) if HAVE[\"few\"] else None\n","SEI = json.loads(_SEI_P.read_text()) if HAVE[\"SEI\"] else {}\n","rag[\"model\"] = rag[\"model\"].str.replace(r\"^kbench/\", \"\", regex=True)\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# PANEL DISCIPLINE — the single most error-prone thing in this dataset\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# Fig 2a/2b are defined on the MATCHED TEN-MODEL panel. That panel can only be\n","# identified from the few-shot file, which lists exactly those ten models.\n","#\n","# If the few-shot file is absent we must NOT substitute some other subset: any\n","# substitute silently yields DIFFERENT, plausible-looking accuracies (the 27-model\n","# panel gives 72.3/60.5/36.2... against the correct 73.3/63.7/39.3...). A wrong\n","# figure is worse than a missing one, so Fig 2 is skipped outright and the reason\n","# is reported. Fig 1/3/4/5 are unaffected — they are defined on the full panel.\n","ALL27 = sorted(set(rag[\"model\"]))\n","if HAVE[\"few\"]:\n","    TEN = sorted(set(few[\"model\"]))\n","    FIG2_OK = True\n","else:\n","    TEN = []\n","    FIG2_OK = False\n","print(f\"panels  : ten-model n={len(TEN) if FIG2_OK else 'n/a (few-shot file absent)'}\"\n","      f\" | rag n={len(ALL27)}\")\n","print(\"figures : Fig1 yes · Fig3 yes · Fig4 yes · Fig5 yes\"\n","      f\" · Fig2 {'yes' if FIG2_OK else 'SKIPPED (needs the ten-model panel)'}\")\n","\n","\n","# ── Wilson 95% CI (matches Section 19) ───────────────────────────────────────\n","def wilson(k: int, n: int, z: float = 1.959963984540054) -> tuple:\n","    if n == 0:\n","        return (np.nan, np.nan)\n","    p = k / n\n","    d = 1 + z * z / n\n","    c = (p + z * z / (2 * n)) / d\n","    h = z * np.sqrt(p * (1 - p) / n + z * z / (4 * n * n)) / d\n","    return (100 * max(0.0, c - h), 100 * min(1.0, c + h))\n","\n","\n","def _acc(d: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple:\n","    k, n = int(d[\"correct\"].sum()), len(d)\n","    return 100 * k / n, n, *wilson(k, n)\n","\n","\n","def _vlabels(ax, xs, vals, hi, *, arm=0, fontsize=6.1):\n","    \"\"\"Value labels above each bar, in a per-arm vertical band.\n","\n","    The CI is already drawn as an error bar, so only the point estimate is\n","    printed — appending \"[lo, hi]\" overprints the neighbouring bars. Each arm of\n","    a grouped triple gets its own band so labels can never collide horizontally.\n","    Returns the topmost label y, for setting y-limits.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    dy = 1.7 + arm * 2.6                              # arm 0 sits closest to its bar\n","    top = 0.0\n","    for x, v, h in zip(xs, vals, hi):\n","        y = h + dy\n","        ax.text(x, y, f\"{v:.1f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\",\n","                fontsize=fontsize, zorder=5)\n","        top = max(top, y)\n","    return top + 2.8\n","\n","\n","# ── derived tables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# Fig 2 uses the matched ten-model panel for BOTH strategies and few-shot. The\n","# few-shot arm requires its own file; without it Fig 2a/2b cannot be built (the\n","# few-shot bars and the \"vs few-shot\" series would be fabricated), so they are\n","# marked unavailable and every other figure still renders.\n","FIG2_OK = HAVE[\"few\"]\n","_NA_T = (float(\"nan\"), 0, np.nan, np.nan)\n","tier_cells = {}\n","for t in TIERS:\n","    tier_cells[t] = {\n","        \"few\":   _acc(few[few.tier == t]) if FIG2_OK else _NA_T,\n","        \"naive\": _acc(rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)])\n","                 if FIG2_OK else _NA_T,\n","        \"rule\":  _acc(rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)])\n","                 if FIG2_OK else _NA_T,\n","    }\n","\n","# Fig 2b — net ADDITIONAL correct pairs, naive->rule and few->rule (300 pairs/tier)\n","net = {}\n","for t in TIERS:\n","    nv = rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)] \\\n","        .set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","    en = rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)] \\\n","        .set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","    j = en.rename(\"en\").to_frame().join(nv.rename(\"nv\"))\n","    if len(j) != 300:\n","        print(f\"  [warn] {t}: expected 300 pairs on the ten-model panel, got {len(j)}\")\n","    net[t] = {\"vs_naive\": int(j.en.sum() - j.nv.sum())}\n","    if FIG2_OK:\n","        fw = few[few.tier == t].set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","        jj = j.join(fw.rename(\"fw\"))\n","        net[t][\"vs_few\"] = int(jj.en.sum() - jj.fw.sum())\n","    else:\n","        net[t][\"vs_few\"] = None\n","\n","# Fig 3 — per-question prompt tokens (constant within a question; 27-model panel)\n","tok = {}\n","for t in TIERS:\n","    b = rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\")][\"prompt_tokens\"]\n","    r = rag[(rag.tier == t) & (rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\")][\"prompt_tokens\"]\n","    tok[t] = (b.mean(), b.std(), r.mean(), r.std())\n","\n","# Fig 4a — was a third table actually delivered?\n","# prompt_tokens is a per-question constant, so a delta vs the naive arm is an\n","# unambiguous signal that rule-augmented retrieved a third table.\n","_qn = rag[rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\"].groupby(\"q_id\")[\"prompt_tokens\"].first()\n","_qr = rag[rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\"].groupby(\"q_id\")[\"prompt_tokens\"].first()\n","_delta = _qr - _qn\n","THREE_Q = set(_delta[_delta != 0].index)\n","deliv = {t: {\"two\": sum(q not in THREE_Q for q in _qn.index if q.startswith(t)),\n","             \"three\": sum(q in THREE_Q for q in _qn.index if q.startswith(t))}\n","         for t in TIERS}\n","\n","# Fig 4b — rule-augmented accuracy, split by tables delivered (27-model panel)\n","en_all = rag[rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\"].copy()\n","en_all[\"grp\"] = np.where(en_all.q_id.isin(THREE_Q), \"three\", \"two\")\n","grp_acc = {t: {\"two\": _acc(en_all[(en_all.tier == t) & (en_all.grp == \"two\")]),\n","               \"three\": _acc(en_all[(en_all.tier == t) & (en_all.grp == \"three\")])}\n","           for t in TIERS}\n","\n","# Fig 5 — per-model slopegraph on the 27-model RAG panel\n","_na = rag[rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\"].groupby(\"model\")[\"correct\"].mean() * 100\n","_ru = rag[rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\"].groupby(\"model\")[\"correct\"].mean() * 100\n","slope = _na.rename(\"naive\").to_frame().join(_ru.rename(\"rule\"))\n","slope[\"delta\"] = slope.rule - slope.naive\n","slope = slope.sort_values(\"delta\")\n","_sd = 1e-9\n","fig5_counts = {\"better\": int((slope.delta > _sd).sum()),\n","               \"same\": int((slope.delta.abs() <= _sd).sum()),\n","               \"worse\": int((slope.delta < -_sd).sum())}\n","\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# FIGURE 1 — evaluation pipeline\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","def fig1():\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7.1, 3.15))\n","    ax.set_axis_off()\n","\n","    def box(x, y, w, h, title, body, fc, tfs=8.2):\n","        ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((x, y), w, h,\n","                                    boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.010,rounding_size=0.018\",\n","                                    fc=fc, ec=\"#333333\", lw=0.9, zorder=2))\n","        ax.text(x + w / 2, y + h - 0.050, title, ha=\"center\", va=\"top\",\n","                fontsize=tfs, fontweight=\"bold\", zorder=3)\n","        ax.text(x + w / 2, y + h - 0.150, body, ha=\"center\", va=\"top\",\n","                fontsize=6.7, zorder=3, linespacing=1.30)\n","\n","    def arrow(x0, y0, x1, y1):\n","        ax.add_patch(FancyArrowPatch((x0, y0), (x1, y1), arrowstyle=\"-|>\",\n","                                     mutation_scale=8.5, lw=0.9, color=\"#333333\",\n","                                     shrinkA=1.5, shrinkB=1.5, zorder=1,\n","                                     connectionstyle=\"arc3,rad=0\"))\n","\n","    LW = 0.215                                     # arm-box width (x-span 0.29->0.505)\n","    # Database → three strategy arms\n","    box(0.010, 0.34, 0.255, 0.52, \"Database\",\n","        \"3 tables\\nsensors · variables · readings\\n(DDL + NL descriptions)\", \"#ededed\")\n","    y_naive, y_rule, y_few = 0.735, 0.360, 0.030\n","    hh = 0.235\n","    box(0.315, y_naive, LW, hh, \"Naïve retrieval\",\n","        \"top-2 chunks by\\nembedding similarity\", \"#dce6f2\")\n","    box(0.315, y_rule, LW, hh, \"Rule-augmented\",\n","        \"same 2 chunks +\\n2 inclusion rules\", \"#f6dcdd\")\n","    box(0.315, y_few, LW, hh, \"Full-schema few-shot\",\n","        \"bare DDL of 3 tables\\n+ 3 worked examples\", \"#e4e4e4\", tfs=7.9)\n","\n","    # Prompt + execution\n","    box(0.590, 0.335, 0.150, 0.53, \"Prompt\",\n","        \"schema\\ncontext\\n+ question\", \"#ffffff\", tfs=8.2)\n","    box(0.795, 0.335, 0.195, 0.53, \"LLM → SQL\",\n","        \"executed against\\nthe frozen\\nSQLite snapshot\", \"#ededed\", tfs=8.2)\n","\n","    # Database → each arm (fan out from the right edge midpoint)\n","    for yc in (y_naive + hh / 2, y_rule + hh / 2, y_few + hh / 2):\n","        arrow(0.266, 0.60, 0.315, yc)\n","    # each arm → Prompt\n","    for yc in (y_naive + hh / 2, y_rule + hh / 2, y_few + hh / 2):\n","        arrow(0.530, yc, 0.590, 0.60)\n","    arrow(0.740, 0.60, 0.795, 0.60)\n","\n","    ax.set_xlim(0, 1)\n","    ax.set_ylim(-0.03, 1.02)\n","    ax.set_title(\"Fig. 1 — Evaluation pipeline: three schema-delivery strategies\",\n","                 fontsize=9.4, pad=7)\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig1_pipeline.pdf\")\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig1_pipeline.png\")\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# FIGURE 2 — accuracy by tier + net additional correct pairs\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","def fig2():\n","    fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(7.1, 2.95))\n","\n","    # ── (a) grouped bars with Wilson 95% CI ──\n","    x = np.arange(len(TIERS))\n","    w = 0.26\n","    arms = [(\"few\", C_FEW, \"Few-shot\"), (\"naive\", C_NAIVE, \"Naïve retrieval\"),\n","            (\"rule\", C_RULE, \"Rule-augmented\")]\n","    if not FIG2_OK:\n","        arms = [a for a in arms if a[0] != \"few\"]\n","        w = 0.34\n","    _ymax = 0.0\n","    for i, (key, col, lbl) in enumerate(arms):\n","        vals = np.array([tier_cells[t][key][0] for t in TIERS])\n","        lo = np.array([tier_cells[t][key][2] for t in TIERS])\n","        hi = np.array([tier_cells[t][key][3] for t in TIERS])\n","        _x = x + (i - (len(arms) - 1) / 2) * w\n","        ax1.bar(_x, vals, w, label=lbl, color=col,\n","                edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","        ax1.errorbar(_x, vals, yerr=[vals - lo, hi - vals], fmt=\"none\",\n","                     ecolor=\"#222222\", elinewidth=0.8, capsize=2.2, zorder=3)\n","        _ymax = max(_ymax, _vlabels(ax1, _x, vals, hi, arm=i))\n","    ax1.set_xticks(x)\n","    ax1.set_xticklabels(TIER_LBL)\n","    ax1.set_ylabel(\"Execution accuracy (%)\")\n","    ax1.set_ylim(0, _ymax + 6.0)\n","    ax1.set_title(\"(a) Accuracy by tier and strategy (95% Wilson CI)\", fontsize=8.8)\n","    ax1.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"lower center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.36),\n","               ncol=3, fontsize=7.0, handlelength=1.3, columnspacing=1.0)\n","    ax1.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.4, alpha=0.35, zorder=0)\n","    ax1.set_axisbelow(True)\n","\n","    # ── (b) net additional correct pairs ──\n","    nv = np.array([net[t][\"vs_naive\"] for t in TIERS])\n","    ax2.axhline(0, color=\"#333333\", lw=0.9, zorder=3)\n","    ax2.bar(x - (w / 1.6 if FIG2_OK else 0.0), nv, w * 1.2, label=\"vs naïve\", color=C_NAIVE,\n","            edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","    for xi, vi in zip(x - (w / 1.6 if FIG2_OK else 0.0), nv):\n","        ax2.text(xi, vi + (1.0 if vi >= 0 else -2.6), f\"{vi:+d}\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=6.4)\n","    _lo2, _hi2 = -15, 30\n","    if FIG2_OK:\n","        fw = np.array([net[t][\"vs_few\"] for t in TIERS])\n","        ax2.bar(x + w / 1.6, fw, w * 1.2, label=\"vs few-shot\", color=C_FEW,\n","                edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","        for xi, vi in zip(x + w / 1.6, fw):\n","            ax2.text(xi, vi + (1.0 if vi >= 0 else -2.6), f\"{vi:+d}\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=6.4)\n","    else:\n","        ax2.text(0.5, 0.94, \"few-shot file not attached — 'vs few-shot' series omitted\",\n","                 transform=ax2.transAxes, ha=\"center\", fontsize=6.0, color=\"#888888\")\n","    ax2.set_xticks(x)\n","    ax2.set_xticklabels(TIER_LBL)\n","    ax2.set_ylabel(\"Net additional correct pairs (of 300)\")\n","    ax2.set_ylim(_lo2, _hi2)\n","    ax2.set_title(\"(b) Net gain of rule-augmented retrieval, by tier\", fontsize=8.8)\n","    ax2.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"upper left\")\n","    ax2.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.4, alpha=0.35, zorder=0)\n","    ax2.set_axisbelow(True)\n","\n","    fig.tight_layout()\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig2_tier_accuracy_and_net.pdf\")\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig2_tier_accuracy_and_net.png\")\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# FIGURE 3 — schema-context tokens\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","def fig3():\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 3.05))\n","    x = np.arange(len(TIERS))\n","    bm = np.array([tok[t][0] for t in TIERS])\n","    bs = np.array([tok[t][1] for t in TIERS])\n","    rm = np.array([tok[t][2] for t in TIERS])\n","    rs = np.array([tok[t][3] for t in TIERS])\n","\n","    ax.errorbar(x - 0.035, bm, yerr=bs, marker=\"o\", ms=4.4, lw=1.5, capsize=3,\n","                color=C_NAIVE, label=\"Naïve retrieval\", zorder=3)\n","    ax.errorbar(x + 0.035, rm, yerr=rs, marker=\"s\", ms=4.4, lw=1.5, capsize=3,\n","                color=C_RULE, label=\"Rule-augmented\", zorder=3)\n","\n","    # Bare DDL of all three tables — the paper's Figure 3 reference line.\n","    # NOTE: the paper labels this ≈179 tokens (est.); n4_rho_analysis.json\n","    # reports schema_token_count = 136 for the tokenised DDL. Both are drawn so\n","    # the discrepancy is visible rather than hidden.\n","    # Bare DDL of all three tables — the paper's Figure 3 reference line.\n","    # The paper labels this ≈179 tokens (est.); n4_rho_analysis.json reports a\n","    # tokenised schema_token_count of 136. The two are NOT the same quantity, so\n","    # only the paper's line is drawn and the other is stated in the note.\n","    ddl_est = 179\n","    ddl_meas = SEI.get(\"schema_token_count\", 136)\n","    ax.axhline(ddl_est, ls=\"--\", lw=0.9, color=\"#333333\", zorder=1)\n","    # Label in the right margin, clear of every data mark.\n","    ax.text(4.58, ddl_est, f\"Bare DDL\\n(≈{ddl_est}, est.)\", fontsize=6.0,\n","            ha=\"left\", va=\"center\", color=\"#333333\", zorder=4, linespacing=1.25)\n","    # Footnote in the empty lower-left corner.\n","    ax.text(-0.42, 151.0,\n","            f\"tokenised schema_token_count = {ddl_meas} (n4_rho_analysis.json)\",\n","            fontsize=5.6, ha=\"left\", va=\"bottom\", color=\"#777777\", zorder=4)\n","\n","    ax.set_xticks(x)\n","    ax.set_xticklabels(TIER_LBL)\n","    ax.set_xlim(-0.45, 5.05)\n","    ax.set_ylabel(\"Schema-context tokens per question\")\n","    ax.set_ylim(148, 288)\n","    ax.set_title(\"Fig. 3 — Schema-context tokens by tier (mean ±1 SD)\", fontsize=9.0)\n","    ax.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"upper left\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.005, 1.0))\n","    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.4, alpha=0.35, zorder=0)\n","    ax.set_axisbelow(True)\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig3_tokens.pdf\")\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig3_tokens.png\")\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# FIGURE 4 — where the rules fired + accuracy by tables delivered\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","def fig4():\n","    fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(7.1, 2.95))\n","    x = np.arange(len(TIERS))\n","\n","    # ── (a) 2 vs 3 tables delivered ──\n","    two = np.array([deliv[t][\"two\"] for t in TIERS])\n","    three = np.array([deliv[t][\"three\"] for t in TIERS])\n","    ax1.bar(x, two, 0.55, label=\"two tables (rule did not fire)\", color=C_NAIVE,\n","            edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","    ax1.bar(x, three, 0.55, bottom=two, label=\"three tables (rule added one)\",\n","            color=C_RULE, edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","    for xi, t2, t3 in zip(x, two, three):\n","        if t2:\n","            ax1.text(xi, t2 / 2, str(int(t2)), ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n","                     fontsize=7.0, color=\"white\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n","        if t3:\n","            ax1.text(xi, t2 + t3 / 2, str(int(t3)), ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n","                     fontsize=7.0, color=\"white\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n","    ax1.set_xticks(x)\n","    ax1.set_xticklabels(TIER_LBL)\n","    ax1.set_ylabel(\"Questions (of 30)\")\n","    ax1.set_ylim(0, 34)\n","    ax1.set_title(\"(a) Tables delivered by rule-augmented retrieval\", fontsize=8.8)\n","    ax1.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"lower center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.30),\n","               ncol=2, fontsize=7.0, handlelength=1.3, columnspacing=1.2)\n","    ax1.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.4, alpha=0.35, zorder=0)\n","    ax1.set_axisbelow(True)\n","\n","    # ── (b) accuracy split by tables delivered (27-model panel) ──\n","    w = 0.34\n","    _ymax = 0.0\n","    for i, (key, col, lbl) in enumerate([(\"two\", C_NAIVE, \"two tables\"),\n","                                         (\"three\", C_RULE, \"three tables\")]):\n","        vals = np.array([grp_acc[t][key][0] for t in TIERS])\n","        lo = np.array([grp_acc[t][key][2] for t in TIERS])\n","        hi = np.array([grp_acc[t][key][3] for t in TIERS])\n","        # offset bars within the tier so the 2-table / 3-table pair never touch\n","        _x = x + (i - 0.5) * w\n","        ax2.bar(_x, vals, w, label=lbl, color=col,\n","                edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5, zorder=2)\n","        ax2.errorbar(_x, vals, yerr=[vals - lo, hi - vals],\n","                     fmt=\"none\", ecolor=\"#222222\", elinewidth=0.8, capsize=2.2, zorder=3)\n","        _ymax = max(_ymax, _vlabels(ax2, _x, vals, hi, arm=i))\n","    ax2.set_xticks(x)\n","    ax2.set_xticklabels(TIER_LBL)\n","    ax2.set_ylabel(\"Rule-augmented accuracy (%)\")\n","    ax2.set_ylim(0, _ymax + 6.0)\n","    ax2.set_title(\"(b) Rule-augmented accuracy by tables delivered\", fontsize=8.8)\n","    ax2.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"lower center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.30),\n","               ncol=2, fontsize=7.0, handlelength=1.3, columnspacing=1.2)\n","    ax2.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.4, alpha=0.35, zorder=0)\n","    ax2.set_axisbelow(True)\n","\n","    fig.tight_layout()\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig4_tables_delivered.pdf\")\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig4_tables_delivered.png\")\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# FIGURE 5 — per-model slopegraph (27-model panel)\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","def fig5():\n","    d = slope.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"model\"})\n","    n = len(d)\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.35, 5.1))\n","\n","    # A true slopegraph: ONE shared accuracy axis, one line per model.\n","    # The 27-model panel is dense (22 models improve by 0.7-4.7 pp), so lines are\n","    # drawn thin with slight transparency — the fan of red is itself the finding.\n","    for row in d.itertuples():\n","        dl = row.delta\n","        if dl > _sd:\n","            col, lw, al = \"#c44e52\", 1.25, 0.85\n","        elif dl < -_sd:\n","            col, lw, al = \"#111111\", 1.45, 0.95\n","        else:\n","            col, lw, al = \"#999999\", 1.25, 0.85\n","        ax.plot([0, 1], [row.naive, row.rule], color=col, lw=lw, alpha=al,\n","                marker=\"o\", ms=2.6, zorder=3, solid_capstyle=\"round\")\n","\n","    # Label both endpoints, staggered to avoid overprint, brightest lines on top.\n","    lab = d.sort_values(\"delta\", ascending=True)          # draw decliners last\n","    for row in d.itertuples():\n","        ax.text(-0.045, row.naive, f\"{row.naive:.0f}\", fontsize=5.2, ha=\"right\",\n","                va=\"center\", color=\"#444444\")\n","        ax.text(1.045, row.rule, f\"{row.rule:.0f}\", fontsize=5.2, ha=\"left\",\n","                va=\"center\", color=\"#444444\")\n","\n","    # Right-hand delta column, printed as a clean ranked table beside the graph.\n","    for i, row in enumerate(d.itertuples()):\n","        col = (\"#c44e52\" if row.delta > _sd else\n","               \"#111111\" if row.delta < -_sd else \"#999999\")\n","        y = row.rule\n","        ax.text(1.30, y, f\"{row.delta:+.1f}\", fontsize=5.2, ha=\"right\",\n","                va=\"center\", color=col, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","\n","    ax.set_xticks([0, 1])\n","    ax.set_xticklabels([\"Naïve\\nretrieval\", \"Rule-\\naugmented\"], fontsize=8)\n","    ax.set_xlim(-0.22, 1.42)\n","    ax.set_ylabel(\"Execution accuracy (%)\", fontsize=8)\n","    ax.set_title(\"Fig. 5 — Per-model execution accuracy\\n(27-model panel)\", fontsize=9.0, pad=8)\n","    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.35, alpha=0.3, zorder=0)\n","    ax.set_axisbelow(True)\n","\n","    from matplotlib.lines import Line2D\n","    ax.legend(handles=[Line2D([], [], color=\"#c44e52\", lw=2.0, marker=\"o\", ms=3.4,\n","                              label=f\"improved ({fig5_counts['better']})\"),\n","                       Line2D([], [], color=\"#999999\", lw=2.0, marker=\"o\", ms=3.4,\n","                              label=f\"no change ({fig5_counts['same']})\"),\n","                       Line2D([], [], color=\"#111111\", lw=2.0, marker=\"o\", ms=3.4,\n","                              label=f\"declined ({fig5_counts['worse']})\")],\n","              frameon=False, loc=\"lower center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.155),\n","              ncol=3, fontsize=6.6, handlelength=1.5, columnspacing=1.1)\n","    fig.tight_layout()\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig5_per_model_slope.pdf\")\n","    fig.savefig(_FIG / \"fig5_per_model_slope.png\")\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","\n","\n","# ── render, then write a LaTeX table + a JSON sidecar for the paper ──────────\n","# ── render, then write a LaTeX table + a JSON sidecar for the paper ──────────\n","fig1()\n","if FIG2_OK:\n","    fig2()\n","else:\n","    print(\"[note] Fig 2 skipped — few_shot_rerun_kbench_results.csv is not attached.\")\n","fig3(); fig4(); fig5()\n","\n","# ── manuscripts-name aliases ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# The manuscript references \\includegraphics{figures/fig_<name>.pdf}. Alongside\n","# the descriptive filenames above, emit copies under the paper's exact names so\n","# the manuscript and this notebook can never drift apart or be mis-mapped.\n","import shutil as _sh\n","_ALIAS = {\"fig3_tokens\": \"fig_prompt_tokens\",\n","          \"fig5_per_model_slope\": \"fig_cost_accuracy\"}\n","for _stem, _alias in _ALIAS.items():\n","    for _ext in (\".pdf\", \".png\"):\n","        _src_f = _FIG / f\"{_stem}{_ext}\"\n","        if _src_f.exists():\n","            _sh.copy2(_src_f, _FIG / f\"{_alias}{_ext}\")\n","print(\"[figures] manuscript-named copies: \"\n","      + \", \".join(f\"{a}.pdf\" for a in _ALIAS.values()))\n","\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# Paired inference — the numbers the paper leaves as [PENDING]\n","# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# Exact McNemar (two-sided binomial on the discordant cells), matching Section 19.\n","# Reported per tier AND overall, for all three strategy contrasts, plus the\n","# number of DISTINCT questions behind the discordant pairs — the paper asks for\n","# this explicitly (\"the discordant pairs came from [PENDING] distinct questions\").\n","from scipy.stats import binomtest\n","\n","\n","def _mcnemar(a: pd.Series, b: pd.Series) -> dict:\n","    j = a.rename(\"a\").to_frame().join(b.rename(\"b\"))\n","    n_b = int(((j.a == 1) & (j.b == 0)).sum())     # a right, b wrong\n","    n_c = int(((j.a == 0) & (j.b == 1)).sum())     # a wrong, b right\n","    if n_b + n_c == 0:\n","        return {\"b\": 0, \"c\": 0, \"p\": float(\"nan\"), \"or\": float(\"nan\"), \"n_disc\": 0}\n","    p = float(binomtest(n_b, n_b + n_c, 0.5).pvalue)\n","    or_ = float(\"inf\") if n_c == 0 else n_b / n_c\n","    return {\"b\": n_b, \"c\": n_c, \"p\": p, \"or\": or_, \"n_disc\": n_b + n_c}\n","\n","\n","def _pairs(tier: str, strat: str, panel: list) -> pd.Series:\n","    d = rag[(rag.tier == tier) & (rag.strategy == strat) & rag.model.isin(panel)]\n","    return d.set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","\n","\n","CONTRASTS = {\"rule_vs_naive\": (\"enhanced_rag\", \"naive_rag\"),\n","             \"rule_vs_few\":   (\"enhanced_rag\", \"few_shot\"),\n","             \"naive_vs_few\":  (\"naive_rag\", \"few_shot\")}\n","if not FIG2_OK:                       # the two few-shot contrasts need its file\n","    CONTRASTS = {\"rule_vs_naive\": (\"enhanced_rag\", \"naive_rag\")}\n","\n","mcnemar = {}\n","for t in TIERS:\n","    mcnemar[t] = {}\n","    for name, (sa, sb) in CONTRASTS.items():\n","        a = _pairs(t, sa, TEN)\n","        b = (few[few.tier == t].set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","             if sb == \"few_shot\" else _pairs(t, sb, TEN))\n","        mcnemar[t][name] = _mcnemar(a, b)\n","\n","# Whole-panel contrasts\n","all_a = rag[(rag.strategy == \"enhanced_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)].set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","all_b = rag[(rag.strategy == \"naive_rag\") & rag.model.isin(TEN)].set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","mcnemar[\"overall\"] = {\"rule_vs_naive\": _mcnemar(all_a, all_b)}\n","if FIG2_OK:\n","    all_f = few.set_index([\"q_id\", \"model\"])[\"correct\"]\n","    mcnemar[\"overall\"][\"rule_vs_few\"] = _mcnemar(all_a, all_f)\n","    mcnemar[\"overall\"][\"naive_vs_few\"] = _mcnemar(all_b, all_f)\n","else:\n","    # No matched panel => no within-tier inference. Emitting NaN rows would look\n","    # like a computed result, so the block is dropped and the reason stated.\n","    mcnemar = {}\n","\n","# Tier-5 advantage: which questions actually drive it?\n","_t5 = TIERS[-1]\n","t5_advantage = None\n","if FIG2_OK:\n","    _j5 = _pairs(_t5, \"enhanced_rag\", TEN).rename(\"en\").to_frame().join(\n","        _pairs(_t5, \"naive_rag\", TEN).rename(\"nv\"))\n","    _won = _j5[(_j5.en == 1) & (_j5.nv == 0)]\n","    t5_advantage = {\"pairs\": int(len(_won)),\n","                    \"distinct_questions\": int(_won.reset_index()[\"q_id\"].nunique()),\n","                    \"mean_tokens_naive\": float(tok[_t5][0]),\n","                    \"mean_tokens_rule\": float(tok[_t5][2])}\n","\n","if mcnemar:\n","    print(\"\\n── Paired McNemar (exact, ten-model panel) ──\")\n","    for t in list(TIERS) + [\"overall\"]:\n","        for name in CONTRASTS:\n","            m = mcnemar[t][name]\n","            _or = \"inf\" if m[\"or\"] == float(\"inf\") else f\"{m['or']:.2f}\"\n","            print(f\"  {t:7s} {name:13s} b={m['b']:3d} c={m['c']:3d} \"\n","                  f\"p={m['p']:.4g}  OR={_or}\")\n","    print(f\"\\n  Tier-5 advantage ({t5_advantage['pairs']} pairs) comes from \"\n","          f\"{t5_advantage['distinct_questions']} distinct questions\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"\\n[note] paired McNemar skipped — it is defined on the ten-model panel.\")\n","print(f\"  Mean prompt tokens: naive {rag[rag.strategy=='naive_rag'].prompt_tokens.mean():.0f}\"\n","      f\"  rule {rag[rag.strategy=='enhanced_rag'].prompt_tokens.mean():.0f}\")\n","\n","# ── integrity guard: warn loudly if the DB is not the frozen one ─────────────\n","# The paper's figures require the FROZEN snapshot (1,411 / 112 / 87,962 rows).\n","# Section 8 mounts that archive read-only and never rebuilds it, but a\n","# substituted or partially-restored DB still drifts (1,412 / 114 / ~85.7k\n","# readings) and every re-scored number shifts with it. Fail loudly rather than\n","# silently publishing figures computed against the wrong schema.\n","_db = next((p for p in (_ROOT / \"data_export\" / \"urban_observatory.db\",\n","                        _ROOT / \"urban_observatory.db\") if p.exists()), None)\n","if _db is not None:\n","    try:\n","        import sqlite3\n","        _c = sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{_db}?mode=ro\", uri=True)\n","        _cnt = {t: _c.execute(f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {t}\").fetchone()[0]\n","                for t in (\"sensors\", \"variables\", \"readings\")}\n","        _c.close()\n","        _EXPECT = {\"sensors\": 1411, \"variables\": 112, \"readings\": 87962}\n","        if _cnt == _EXPECT:\n","            print(f\"\\n[DB OK] frozen snapshot confirmed: {_cnt}\")\n","        else:\n","            print(f\"\\n[DB WARNING] {_db.name} holds {_cnt}\")\n","            print(f\"           the paper's frozen snapshot is {_EXPECT}\")\n","            print(\"           -> this is the REBUILT database. The stored result CSVs are\")\n","            print(\"              the authoritative source for the paper's figures; do NOT\")\n","            print(\"              re-score answers against this DB to reproduce them.\")\n","    except Exception as _e:                                    # pragma: no cover\n","        print(f\"\\n[DB WARNING] could not inspect {_db.name}: {_e}\")\n","\n","if FIG2_OK:\n","    tbl = [\n","        r\"\\begin{table}[htbp]\", r\"\\centering\",\n","        r\"\\caption{Execution accuracy (\\%) by complexity tier on the ten-model panel\"\n","        r\" (n = 300 pairs per cell), with 95\\% Wilson intervals.}\",\n","        r\"\\label{tab:paper2_tier}\", r\"\\small\",\n","        r\"\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\", r\"\\hline\",\n","        r\"Tier & Few-shot & Na\\\"ive retrieval & Rule-augmented \\\\\", r\"\\hline\",\n","    ]\n","    for t in TIERS:\n","        cells = []\n","        for key in (\"few\", \"naive\", \"rule\"):\n","            a, _n, lo, hi = tier_cells[t][key]\n","            cells.append(f\"{a:.1f} [{lo:.1f}, {hi:.1f}]\")\n","        tbl.append(f\"{t} & \" + \" & \".join(cells) + r\" \\\\\")\n","    tbl += [r\"\\hline\", r\"\\end{tabular}\", r\"\\end{table}\"]\n","    (_FIG / \"tab_paper2_tier.tex\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(tbl), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"[note] tab_paper2_tier.tex not written — it reports the ten-model panel.\")\n","\n","sidecar = {\n","    \"fig2a_tier_accuracy\": {t: {k: tier_cells[t][k][0] for k in (\"few\", \"naive\", \"rule\")} for t in TIERS},\n","    \"fig2b_net_pairs\": net,\n","    \"fig3_tokens\": {t: {\"naive_mean\": tok[t][0], \"naive_sd\": tok[t][1],\n","                        \"rule_mean\": tok[t][2], \"rule_sd\": tok[t][3]} for t in TIERS},\n","    \"fig4a_tables_delive